;; The remedies waiver list (waymark-fp62.2.1).
;;
;; A guard that refuses with an :explain sentence and carries neither
;; :remedies nor :open is a dead end: the caller is told why and is
;; not told what to do next. The [remedies] usability policy warns on
;; every one of them. This list holds the dead ends that existed on
;; the day the check landed, so the warning list shows what is NEW.
;;
;; THE LIST ONLY SHRINKS. waymark10.check refuses a waiver that waives
;; nothing — every guard it names now carries :remedies or :open — so
;; a line here dies the day its debt is paid. Clear a waiver by giving
;; its guard the way out, never by editing the sentence around it.
;;
;; A waiver is a map:
;;   :guard   the guard's own name, a keyword. Exact.
;;   :family  a name PREFIX, a string, in place of :guard. One line
;;            covers every guard a parameterized builder mints —
;;            g/require names itself require:<fact>, g/role names
;;            itself role:<token>, and neither instance is spelled
;;            anywhere a list could enumerate.
;;   :kind    optional. Present, the waiver covers that kind only.
;;            Absent, it covers the guard name wherever it is declared,
;;            which is what a guard shared by two kinds of one module
;;            wants.
;;   :bead    required. The bead that will clear it.
;;   :why     optional. One sentence, when the reason is not obvious.
;;
;; The clearing plan is one bead per file, outcome.clj first
;; (waymark-fp62.2's punt). waymark-fp62.2 is the parent every line
;; names until those beads are filed.

[
 ;; ── the framework's parameterized builders (guards.clj) ────────────
 ;; Each of these mints its guards from a call site's argument, so the
 ;; instances have no declaration a list could name. The remedy for
 ;; every one of them is the same shape and none of them carries it:
 ;; the builder itself should take :remedies, and the kinds should
 ;; pass them.
 {:family "require:" :bead "waymark-fp62.2"
  :why "g/require names the missing fact and no door that supplies it."}
